      "by": "rival",
      "claim": "Possible error, inferred from visible info only: on T1 the opponent activated Widow Anchor targeting their own Shizuku, which should negate Shizuku's effects until the end of that turn, yet Shizuku's End Phase effect (#2) was offered and activated that same End Phase. A monster whose effects are negated cannot activate its effects. Opponent hand count (3) also suggests the search added nothing. Please check whether the activation should have been offered. No state correction requested by me.",
      "ruling": {
        "decision": "No error. Negating a monster's effects does not stop it from activating them: the effect is activated and is negated at resolution if the monster is still face-up in the Monster Zone and still negated. Widow Anchor negated Shizuku's effects until the end of the turn, so Shizuku was still negated in that End Phase. Its End Phase effect (a Trigger Effect activated in the Monster Zone) could be activated and resolved negated: no Spell was added and its once per turn was used (that last point is the engine's reading, no Konami page found). The engine offered and resolved it correctly; no state correction.",
